WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.670
- Welcome to another episode
of the Wednesday Checkup.

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.500
Today's topic, COVID-19

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.810
because there's more
confusion than ever before.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:09.480
And I think there are two main
driving factors behind this,

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.980
the media, and two our leadership,

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.790
more specifically, President Trump.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.550
I'll be addressing both of those points

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.700
using several examples in this video.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:18.830
Let's get started.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.750
You don't have a medical background.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.840
You're not a scientist, yet
you're claiming this substance,

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.970
which has not been studied
in any meaningful way

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.570
can cure COVID.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:31.430
And do you have a financial
stake in the company you would

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:34.742
profit from it if this
is being sold widely.

00:00:34.742 --> 00:00:36.683
Morally, is that right?

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.689
- Well, you know, I was contacted
on Easter Sunday after it,

00:00:38.689 --> 00:00:42.932
you know, that I've told
the whole country to pray

00:00:42.932 --> 00:00:44.920
for the answer for this pandemic.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.790
So this guy called me on Easter Sunday

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:48.193
and the city had an answer.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.470
- This is all bologna.

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:54.870
While I am very angry for him coming

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:55.709
out and spewing this
misinformation about oleander

00:00:55.709 --> 00:01:00.709
or Oleandrin oil which is poisonous.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.730
There's actually cardiac
toxicity that comes from this,

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.237
what I'm more upset about is CNN giving

00:01:07.237 --> 00:01:09.320
this person a platform.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:13.070
What was the purpose of bringing
him on and making this into

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:14.960
a national story when it wasn't,

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.700
this actually led to president
Trump being asked this

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.208
question by reporters.

00:01:20.208 --> 00:01:22.000
- [Reporter] Oleandrin?

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.084
Have you heard of that as a possible

00:01:23.084 --> 00:01:24.454
therapy for coronavirus?

00:01:24.454 --> 00:01:25.287
- I've heard about it, yes go ahead.

00:01:25.287 --> 00:01:26.410
- [Reporter] Have you pressed
the FDA to approve it?

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.192
- No I haven't, I haven't.

00:01:28.192 --> 00:01:29.312
- [Reporter] Is it
something you would support?

00:01:29.312 --> 00:01:30.597
- Is it something the people are talking

00:01:30.597 --> 00:01:32.290
about very strongly?

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:33.130
We'll look at it.

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:35.570
- He clearly has no idea
what the reporter is asking.

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.600
And the only reason the
reporter is asking this question

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.980
is because it was seen on CNN.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:42.370
I'm also really upset with CNN
that they're wasting airtime

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:43.203
on Mike Lindell,

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:46.060
where we have great scientists
that have hard hitting

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.050
stories that are really important to tell,

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:51.061
including that the black
population in the United States is

00:01:51.061 --> 00:01:53.820
being disproportionately
affected by COVID-19.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:56.580
That there are certain
difficulties in obtaining tests

00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:59.420
in low socioeconomic
neighborhoods in the US.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:01.300
Why are we talking to the My Pillow guy?

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:05.050
Let's move on to a tweet
that president Trump himself

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:09.940
retweeted stating that only
9,000 people, incorrectly stated

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:13.920
that only 9,000 people have
died of COVID-19 thus far,

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.460
the tweet actually ended up
being removed for violating

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:17.340
terms of service.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.910
But let's talk about where
they got this number from.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:23.360
This 6% figure or 9,000
deaths actually came

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.050
from a legitimate CDC

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:30.050
document that said 94% of the
deaths related to COVID-19 had

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:34.760
several causes of death listed
on the death certificate.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.010
And that's actually not that surprising.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.030
It is very rare for an
individual to have a single thing

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:41.300
listed on their death certificate,

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:42.995
because for those of us
who actually fill out death

00:02:42.995 --> 00:02:46.700
certificates, we know we put
a primary cause of death,

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.110
as well as contributing causes of death.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:52.240
For example, if you have hypertension

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.920
or your BMI falls in the obese category,

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.910
you technically have risk
factors and diagnoses

00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.833
that contributed to your
demise, to your loss of life,

00:03:01.819 --> 00:03:02.652
but COVID-19 is what caused it.

00:03:02.652 --> 00:03:04.860
These are just extra things,
things that made you high risk

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:06.700
and more susceptible to COVID-19.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:11.020
That doesn't mean it wasn't
COVID-19 that led to your death.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:13.280
It's very rare that a
person dies specifically

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.640
of a single illness.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:19.590
So it is completely inaccurate
to say that only 6% of people

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:21.163
died as a result of COVID-19.

00:03:21.163 --> 00:03:25.290
A 100% of those people died
with COVID-19 and from COVID-19.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:28.050
And some of them had extra
things listed on their death

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:30.060
certificate, such as respiratory failure,

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.890
where do they get
respiratory failure from?

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.530
COVID-19.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:35.400
It's misinformation at its finest.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.980
And it causes you to think,

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:39.490
oh, COVID-19 is not as deadly as it looks.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:42.379
COVID-19 takes our most fragile patients.

00:03:42.379 --> 00:03:44.340
And it lead to a high death rate.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.300
It also affects the younger
generations and creates

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.820
complications for them
at a lower death rate,

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:54.030
but still a serious illness
that we must not write off.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:57.430
Let's look at this headline from kpbs.org.

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:01.730
COVID-19 and the brain quote
"You should be afraid".

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:05.020
Now only do I think this is
an absolutely trash headline.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:09.430
It capitalizes on humans being
afraid of COVID-19 in hopes

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.710
that they would click on this article

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:13.490
and read it and they would raise
more money via advertising.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:15.610
I think this is the worst
type of health care reporting

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.100
because it's dishonest.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.660
While we are seeing some longterm

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:21.680
effects related to COVID-19,

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:26.270
we also see longterm effects
of any person that's admitted

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:27.270
into an ICU.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.140
If you're in an ICU for a
heart attack, for diabetic

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:31.493
ketoacidosis, for sepsis coming out

00:04:31.493 --> 00:04:36.493
of that ICU will be a
long recovery process.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:37.870
Your lungs will be scarred.

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:39.870
You will have inflammation in your body.

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:40.703
At certain times,

00:04:40.703 --> 00:04:43.350
you'll have neurological
symptoms, brain fog.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:47.530
This is classic ICU protocol
in coming out of the ICU.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:49.750
It is not the norm to see longterm

00:04:49.750 --> 00:04:51.430
health effects of COVID-19.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:53.830
Most people will get better with COVID-19,

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:55.000
most people will recover

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.610
and not have any serious
long lasting symptoms.

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:59.520
There will be a subset of the population

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:01.450
that will have some lingering symptoms,

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:04.740
just like they do with a
serious case of influenza,

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:07.880
just like they do with us
heart attack or with any other

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.140
of reasonable number of illnesses.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:13.100
The truth is we don't know
what the longterm effects are

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.340
of COVID-19, we're studying them.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.650
And if you ask doctors,
they'll tell you the truth.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:18.483
They'll tell you that

00:05:18.483 --> 00:05:20.530
in some cases they're
seeing effects on the brain,

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:22.654
on the heart and COVID-19 is unique

00:05:22.654 --> 00:05:24.380
because it seems to be affect

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:26.890
different organs throughout
your body, not just your lungs.

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:29.690
But again, this isn't the case
for the majority of cases,

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:32.280
we should not report on
medical stories this way.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.370
A, it causes health care related anxiety,

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:37.400
which I see day in and
day out, especially now.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.060
And two, it's not gonna
change anyone's minds

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.190
that disagrees with you.

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:43.700
The people who think COVID-19
is a hoax will not be

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:46.490
convinced by your
overdramatic news reporting.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.240
There's no reason to do.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.390
Next, let's look at this tweet

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.970
by President Trump on August 22nd.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:54.860
The deep state or whoever over
at the FDA is making it very

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:57.130
difficult for drug companies
to get people in order

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.290
to test the vaccine and therapeutics.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:01.440
Obviously they're hoping to
delay the answer until after

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:04.210
November 3rd, must focus
on speed and saving lives.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:07.287
If you are a president of a
nation and you have at your

00:06:07.287 --> 00:06:09.660
disposal, the FDA, the CDC,

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:12.250
the last thing you
should be doing is trying

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:14.290
to make them look bad.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:17.270
The more you put out into
the public that the FDA

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:20.750
has deep state actors or
the CDC is not being honest,

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.160
whatever it is, you're tweeting.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:25.010
You're losing the faith of
the American people in these

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:27.222
institutions, the scientists and doctors

00:06:27.222 --> 00:06:30.480
that are working day in and
day out at the CDC and FDA.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:33.342
They're not hiding treatments
and letting people die because

00:06:33.342 --> 00:06:37.370
they care about who wins
the presidential election.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.900
What they do care about is
making sure everything's done

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:43.870
with integrity, with scientific
rigor, with accuracy.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.430
And that's how it must continue.

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:47.100
Because guess what President Trump,

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:50.790
when we do have a good vaccine,
that's safe, that works,

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:53.010
you're gonna need the public's
trust in order for them

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.240
to get this vaccine.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.308
And with tweets like that,

00:06:55.308 --> 00:06:57.860
you're making it very, very difficult.

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:01.360
Final point I want to talk
about is schools reopening the

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.980
fact that there's some
infections happening at these

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.070
schools, universities, local institutions.

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:08.330
And I feel like we're approaching
these stories with a lot

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:09.446
of irrationality, a lot of panic.

00:07:09.446 --> 00:07:13.480
Remember my mantra from the
beginning of COVID-19 has been

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:14.930
stay alert, not anxious.

00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:16.820
The reason I say this is
because there's constantly

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:18.585
headlines, University of Alabama

00:07:18.585 --> 00:07:21.000
has over 1,000 cases in a month.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.810
School district in Georgia
has 20 cases of COVID-19.

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:27.660
We're gonna see cases in
schools, in our cities,

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.400
in our states, as we begin
to reopening process.

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.590
The danger with COVID-19 is that it

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:34.380
can spread like wildfire.

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:36.690
And as long as we keep these numbers low,

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:38.060
that's what's important.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.700
We need to protect the population
who is most vulnerable,

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:43.750
and we need to make smart
decisions with good quality data,

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:46.590
not politicize the topic,
not try and scare people.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:49.130
And reality is as we reopen schools,

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:51.610
as we reopen shopping areas, gyms,

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:54.240
we will see a small
spike in COVID-19 cases.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:57.230
It's not about seeing a
small uptick and panicking.

00:07:57.230 --> 00:07:58.710
That's the last thing we want.

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:00.470
Students, let's be mature.

00:08:00.470 --> 00:08:01.880
Let's not throw parties.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.979
- [News Anchor] Tonight,
several Yukon students have been

00:08:03.979 --> 00:08:07.830
evicted from on campus housing
after this packed party.

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:09.900
- Let's not say, forget COVID-19.

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:11.143
- [Group] (beep) coronavirus.

00:08:12.082 --> 00:08:13.590
- I drink Coronas all day.

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:14.750
- I personally think it's a hoax.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:17.920
- Look, odds are, if you're
young and you get COVID-19,

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:19.540
it's not going to be the end of the world,

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.610
but you can potentially spread
it to many other people.

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.170
And when you go to a party, a
room full of a hundred people,

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:28.640
it takes one to get many others
sick who then will travel

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:30.110
home and get many others sick.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:32.350
It's about the speed at which it spreads.

00:08:32.350 --> 00:08:34.630
Focus on school for a
short period of time,

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:38.420
wear a mask at the end of
the day, just be reasonable.

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:41.100
Something really important to
talk about when it comes to

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:46.100
covering COVID-19 is that people
really look down upon those

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:47.560
who are misinformed.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:50.340
And just like I do with
vaccine hesitant parents,

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:52.380
I do not rush to judge them.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:55.880
That is a surefire way to
get them to never your point

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.800
of view, to never understand
truly how science works,

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:00.600
think about how you can connect with them,

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.250
to educate them on why it's not stupid

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.560
and why they should take care.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:06.010
Because right now, as a person,

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:08.500
without a scientific
background, it is confusing.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.028
You do hear contradicting
opinions on the news,

00:09:11.028 --> 00:09:12.790
in our politics.

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:16.010
So media, President Trump
and everyone in between,

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:19.320
let's take a more empathetic
approach here and be smart with

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.220
the things we're putting
out to the general public.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:23.660
We all want the same thing, less deaths,

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.487
a healthier and happier public
and the end of COVID-19.

00:09:26.487 --> 00:09:29.790
And the only way we can get
there is by working together.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.599
You want to check out some of
my other interesting content

00:09:31.599 --> 00:09:35.330
about COVID-19 click here or
for more lighthearted playlists

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:37.780
that I put together a
special for you click here.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:40.245
As always stay happy and healthy.

00:09:40.245 --> 00:09:42.828
(mellow music)

